From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:24:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: edit and delete sent messages from the Messaging app

* Edit sent messages from the Messaging app

The Messaging app can now edit a message the user sent. The transport
emits "webos-im-send-edit" with the account, the chat (a buddy name for
a DM, the channel id for a group DM or server channel), the message's
serviceMessageId and the new text. For Discord that id is the message
snowflake that "webos-im-outbox-id" reported from the gateway echo of
the send.

The handler PATCHes /channels/{channel}/messages/{id} with the new
content and returns TRUE once the request is on its way, FALSE for an
account that is not Discord's or a message whose channel it cannot
find. The channel comes from the message itself where the plug-in has
seen it (msgid_to_channel), otherwise from the chat, the same way the
reaction handler finds it; that lookup moves to a function both use.
The text arrives in the form send_im gets, so it goes through the same
markdown conversion a send does, now a function of its own, and the
same 1..2000 byte bound.

The URL is built by a new webos_helpers.c, which takes no connection
and only accepts a message id made of digits, so nothing else can end
up in the path. tests/ has a unit test for it ("make -C tests check").

* Delete messages from the Messaging app

The Messaging app can now delete a message for everyone. The transport
emits "webos-im-send-delete" with the account, the chat and the
message's serviceMessageId, the Discord message snowflake.

The handler finds the channel as the edit handler does and sends
DELETE /channels/{channel}/messages/{id}. It returns TRUE once the
request is on its way, FALSE for an account that is not Discord's or a
message whose channel it cannot find. Discord itself decides whether
the user may delete the message: their own always, someone else's only
in a server channel where they may manage messages.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
